import ../../../testing/driver.dl

palette daylight colors:
    color "Paper" is UI ink 250 250 249
    color "Text" is UI ink 30 34 40
    color "Accent" is UI ink 130 50 10

palette midnight colors:
    color "Paper" is UI ink 18 24 32
    color "Text" is UI ink 235 240 246
    color "Accent" is UI ink 245 198 91

appearance paper appearance:
    background is palette color "Paper"
    text is palette color "Text"
    accent is palette color "Accent"
    border width is 1
    border is palette color "Accent"
    padding is 12
    gap is 8

appearance emphasis appearance:
    text is palette color "Accent"

appearance editor appearance:
    height is 80

appearance responsive paper appearance:
    use paper appearance
    when viewport is below 400:
        text is palette color "Accent"

document palette preview using responsive paper appearance:
    paragraph "Introduction" using no UI appearance:
        words "See "
        link "the colors" to "/colors" using emphasis appearance
    text surface "Draft" containing "starter" using editor appearance

to require paint {UI paint:actual} equals {UI paint:expected}:
    require condition (((actual's red = expected's red) and (actual's green = expected's green)) and (actual's blue = expected's blue)) reporting "An appearance resolved the wrong palette color"

set first to an instance of palette preview
set second to an instance of palette preview
set window to the address of first
use UI palette daylight colors in window
use UI palette midnight colors in (the address of second)
set view to a UI view of window sized 500 by 400 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
set other to a UI view of (the address of second) sized 500 by 400 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
# Start outside the windows so initial hover discovery cannot request a paint.
set view's cursor and other's cursor to a UI point at -1.0 and -1.0
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of other)
require paint (view's layout's appearance's background) equals (UI ink 250 250 249)
require paint (view's layout's appearance's foreground) equals (UI ink 30 34 40)
require paint (view's layout's appearance's accent) equals (UI ink 130 50 10)
require paint (view's layout's appearance's border ink) equals (UI ink 130 50 10)
require paint (other's layout's appearance's background) equals (UI ink 18 24 32)
require paint (other's layout's appearance's accent) equals (UI ink 245 198 91)
set link to the UI layout labeled "the colors" in (view's layout)
require paint (link's appearance's foreground) equals (UI ink 130 50 10)

set revision to first's revision
set surface to view's window as a pointer to test UI surface
set paints to surface's paints
use UI palette daylight colors in window
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition ((first's revision = revision) and (surface's paints = paints)) reporting "Selecting the same palette repainted an unchanged view"

set value to the UI value for (the control labeled "Draft" in window) in window
set draft to the UI layout labeled "Draft" in (view's layout)
activate UI layout draft in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 3 key 65 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 2 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 4 key 0 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "kept draft" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 3 key 65 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 2 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition ((the selected UI text in (the address of view)) = "kept draft") reporting "The palette fixture did not select its edited draft"
set history to value's undo
use UI palette midnight colors in window
require condition (first's revision > revision) reporting "A palette change did not invalidate its views"
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require paint (view's layout's appearance's background) equals (UI ink 18 24 32)
require paint (view's layout's appearance's foreground) equals (UI ink 235 240 246)
require paint (draft's appearance's accent) equals (UI ink 245 198 91)
require paint (link's appearance's foreground) equals (UI ink 245 198 91)
require condition ((value's text = "kept draft") and (value's undo = history)) reporting "Changing a palette replaced an editor draft or its undo history"
require condition ((the selected UI text in (the address of view)) = "kept draft") reporting "Changing a palette moved the editor selection"

set view's width to 320
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require paint (view's layout's appearance's foreground) equals (UI ink 245 198 91)
require paint (other's layout's appearance's foreground) equals (UI ink 235 240 246)
close the address of view
close the address of other
close window
close the address of second
print line "Named palettes resolve inherited, responsive and inline colors per instance without replacing editor state or repainting unchanged selections."
